From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bjarne <87858321+bjakra@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:12:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] OBSERVE_SENSOR_PRIVACY: also privileged

Lets an allowlisted privileged app (Graphite Now Playing) read whether
the microphone privacy toggle is on, as Ambient Music Mod does through
the shell user. Read-only; MANAGE_SENSOR_PRIVACY is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 core/res/AndroidManifest.xml | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml b/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml
index d49a48f8d11b1bbecfdb94659af2eb131f901c57..240d83d708fc8380488c94ebf9e9b421d669b21c 100644
--- a/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -9206,9 +9206,11 @@
                 android:protectionLevel="internal|role|installer" />
 
     <!-- @SystemApi Allows sensor privacy changes to be observed.
+         Graphite: also privileged, so an allowlisted privileged app (Graphite Now Playing) can read
+         whether the microphone toggle is on. Read-only; changing it still needs MANAGE_SENSOR_PRIVACY.
          @hide -->
     <permission android:name="android.permission.OBSERVE_SENSOR_PRIVACY"
-                android:protectionLevel="internal|role|installer"
+                android:protectionLevel="internal|role|installer|privileged"
                 android:permissionFlags="allowedInPrivateComputeCore" />
 
     <!-- @SystemApi Permission that protects the {@link Intent#ACTION_REVIEW_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICES}
From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bjarne <87858321+bjakra@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:29:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Sensor privacy: let Graphite Now Playing read the toggles,
 permission unchanged

Making OBSERVE_SENSOR_PRIVACY privileged meant every privileged app that
already requests it (SystemUI, Shell, PermissionController) needed a
privapp allowlist entry; a user build would refuse to boot without them.
The permission keeps its protection level; instead the sensor privacy
service accepts the preinstalled org.graphite.nowplaying for reading,
the same way it exempts SystemUI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 core/res/AndroidManifest.xml                             | 4 +---
 .../server/sensorprivacy/SensorPrivacyService.java       | 9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml b/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml
index 240d83d708fc8380488c94ebf9e9b421d669b21c..d49a48f8d11b1bbecfdb94659af2eb131f901c57 100644
--- a/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -9206,11 +9206,9 @@
                 android:protectionLevel="internal|role|installer" />
 
     <!-- @SystemApi Allows sensor privacy changes to be observed.
-         Graphite: also privileged, so an allowlisted privileged app (Graphite Now Playing) can read
-         whether the microphone toggle is on. Read-only; changing it still needs MANAGE_SENSOR_PRIVACY.
          @hide -->
     <permission android:name="android.permission.OBSERVE_SENSOR_PRIVACY"
-                android:protectionLevel="internal|role|installer|privileged"
+                android:protectionLevel="internal|role|installer"
                 android:permissionFlags="allowedInPrivateComputeCore" />
 
     <!-- @SystemApi Permission that protects the {@link Intent#ACTION_REVIEW_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICES}
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/sensorprivacy/SensorPrivacyService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/sensorprivacy/SensorPrivacyService.java
index 792d8fff62b1479d298fa479cc5cdba0380783b9..ceb3fee1bde83464f8615876e9782d33c8d16199 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/sensorprivacy/SensorPrivacyService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/sensorprivacy/SensorPrivacyService.java
@@ -1250,6 +1250,15 @@ public final class SensorPrivacyService extends SystemService {
                 // b/221782106, possible race condition with role grant might bootloop device.
                 return;
             }
+            // Graphite: Graphite Now Playing (preinstalled system app only) may read whether the
+            // microphone toggle is on, like Ambient Music Mod did through the shell user. Reading
+            // only; changing it still needs MANAGE_SENSOR_PRIVACY.
+            int nowPlayingAppId = UserHandle.getAppId(mPackageManagerInternal
+                    .getPackageUid("org.graphite.nowplaying", MATCH_SYSTEM_ONLY,
+                            UserHandle.USER_SYSTEM));
+            if (nowPlayingAppId >= 0 && UserHandle.getCallingAppId() == nowPlayingAppId) {
+                return;
+            }
             if (mContext.checkCallingOrSelfPermission(
                     android.Manifest.permission.OBSERVE_SENSOR_PRIVACY) == PERMISSION_GRANTED) {
                 return;
